  "title": "# Build: ui-asset-designer (Fable phase first) ## Brett said (verbatim) \"We're gonna build a UI ass…",
  "asked": "# Build: ui-asset-designer (Fable phase first) ## Brett said (verbatim) \"We're gonna build a UI asset designer, which will create assets with their manifest and their identifier. It's going to create separate plugins for the app menu designer, the nav menu designer, the toolbar designer, the banner designer, the embedded widget designer, the widget designer. These are not dependent on the designer, but the designer interface will inherit those other designers. The UI designer plugin will have add-ons, each with their own settings interface and the designer's interface.\" \"Redo them all from scratch.\" \"Make it a build and get the Fable stuff going. Make it super powerful: full-blown context menu, drag and drop, map-based. Every UI asset will also have a context menu section which gives you a preview of the UI, and informs you in multiple ways (tooltips etc).\" Full plan + all addenda: Plan Studio plan proposed-fzf3 (Assets section). Read it first. THIS RUN (Fable, max thinking): 1. designer@1 contract: host plugin + add-on model (id, asset type, designer UI, settings UI asset, manifest schema, capabilities). Standalone or inside the host. 2. Asset output contract: manifest + stable identifier, registration in the asset library and UI registry (coordinate with running ui-registry-shortcuts; don't duplicate). 3. Interaction contract for every designer: full context menu, drag and drop, map/canvas-based layout, undo/redo, multi-select. 4. UI asset context-menu section: every UI asset gets a context-menu section with a live preview of the UI and info shown multiple ways (tooltip, hover card, side panel, help text). 5. Fixtures, validators, checks, PORTING.md, report. Write the Opus phase as ~10-min steps in the plan (one add-on per group of steps: App menu, Nav menu, Toolbar, Banner, Embed, Widget; host UI; voice + API/MCP/CLI; 3+ preview options each to UI Review). 6. All from scratch: old banner-editor / designer code is reference only. PR to the merge queue. Do NOT land directly. One session, lean chain. Stay out of Gizmo, badges/notifications, settings, plan-studio builds' code. Watch live: Brett can watch the screen you are changing hot-render in the console. Whenever you start work on a screen or element, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"<what you are changing>\"` (apps: console-web, axhub-web, amberx-droid, walkthrough-studio, demo, framework, console, axhub-android, voicevault). Agent cap: heavy steps (pnpm/npm/vite builds, docker node:22 test runs, Playwright) share a VPS-wide lock. Run each one as `node /opt/axf/deploy/../framework/cli/agent-slots.mjs heavy -- <command>` so only a few run at once. Model switches: a downgrade (e.g. Fable → Opus) is fine. Fable upgrades need no approval right now (Brett, Nov 4 2026: \"If it needs Fable, set it to be Fable\"): a step that needs Fable (schemas, asset types, contracts, engines/kernel, cross-app protocols) is set to Fable and runs on Fable; the switch is recorded on the build. Never launch a step on a higher model than it is pinned to: raise the step first.",
